---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/site.css";
import "../styles/questions.css";
---
<Base
  title="Questions · Meridian"
  description="Plain answers to what finance, audit, procurement and IT security ask about Meridian first, with what is built today marked apart from what is planned."
  share="og-questions.png"
  shareAlt="Meridian: Questions evaluators ask. How to read the answers: Today means in the product now, Planned means on the roadmap."
>

<main id="main">

<!-- 1 · Hero: words left, how to read the answers right -->
<section class="qhero" id="top"><div class="in qhero-grid">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <span class="pill">Questions</span>
    <h1>Questions <em>evaluators ask.</em></h1>
    <p class="lead">What finance, audit, procurement and IT security ask us first. Plain answers, with what is built today marked apart from what is planned.</p>
    <div class="btns"><a class="btn" href="#all">Read the answers</a><a class="btn ghost" href="/request-a-walkthrough">Ask us in a walkthrough</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="qkey mint pv halo"><span class="sheet" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="card qkey-c"><b class="ttl">How to read the answers</b>
      <ul><li><span class="st">Today</span><span>In the product now</span></li><li><span class="st v">Planned</span><span>On the roadmap, not built yet</span></li></ul>
      <div class="rec-f"><span>20 questions</span><span>5 topics</span></div></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- 2 · The answers: topics on the left; on the right, one column that opens a question at a time -->
<section class="sec" id="all" aria-labelledby="h-all"><div class="in acols">
  <div class="ahead">
    <h2 id="h-all" class="rv">Pick a <em>topic.</em></h2>
    <div class="qtabs rv" id="qtabs" role="group" aria-label="Topics"><button type="button" class="qtab" data-g="scope" aria-pressed="true"><span>Scope and fit</span><i>4</i></button><button type="button" class="qtab" data-g="money" aria-pressed="false"><span>Money</span><i>4</i></button><button type="button" class="qtab" data-g="people" aria-pressed="false"><span>People and AI</span><i>4</i></button><button type="button" class="qtab" data-g="security" aria-pressed="false"><span>Security and data</span><i>4</i></button><button type="button" class="qtab" data-g="connect" aria-pressed="false"><span>Connections</span><i>4</i></button></div>
  </div>
  <div class="acc" id="qacc">
    <div class="qg" id="g-scope" data-g="scope"><p class="qgh">Scope and fit</p>
      <details id="q-portal" name="q" open><summary><h3>We already have MDF in our partner portal. Why Meridian?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Partner portal MDF modules usually cover the request, the approval and the claim. The agreement and the purchase order are often handled elsewhere, in procurement or by email, and the invoice is often checked by hand against the approved amount.</p><p>Meridian keeps the agreement, the purchase order, the claim review and the invoice check on the same record as the approval, and enforces the rules between them. Your portal keeps doing deal registration, content and training.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-built" name="q"><summary><h3>What is built today, and what is planned?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Everything on this site is in the product today unless it is marked Planned.</p><p><span class="st v">Planned</span> Five connections to your own systems: sign-in, documents, e-signature, CRM and budget planning. <a class="lk" href="/how-it-works#connect">See what's planned <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></details>
      <details id="q-start" name="q"><summary><h3>Can we start small?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Yes. Start with one region and one Program. A new region or a new year is a setup task: a Workspace, a Program and the people who work in it.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-setup" name="q"><summary><h3>Who sets it up?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Meridian staff set up your organization. Your program administrator then publishes your settings: the calendar, lists, request form, approval route, request numbering and accounts payable address.</p></div></details>
    </div>
    <div class="qg" id="g-money" data-g="money"><p class="qgh">Money</p>
      <details id="q-paid" name="q"><summary><h3>Do you pay our partners?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>No. Meridian never moves money. Approved invoices go to your accounts payable address, stamped with who approved them, and your finance system pays them.</p><p>Meridian records the payment status, so the partner is told.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-currency" name="q"><summary><h3>How are currencies converted?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>At your own monthly exchange rates, which your program administrator uploads. Finance can reproduce every converted figure.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-over" name="q"><summary><h3>What stops an overpayment?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Your claims team reviews each proof file and cost line, then confirms one amount. The invoice must equal that amount exactly, or the claim can't be approved. <a class="lk" href="/controls#c-11">See the rule <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></details>
      <details id="q-budget" name="q"><summary><h3>Can we see budget against spend?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p><span class="st">Today</span> Each Program has an allocation, shown against approved and in-review amounts. Each request records its cost, the co-funding share and the pipeline it is expected to create, so you see the expected return before you approve.</p><p><span class="st v">Planned</span> Budget planning with pools and allocation scenarios, and actual pipeline from your CRM for performance reporting.</p></div></details>
    </div>
    <div class="qg" id="g-people" data-g="people"><p class="qgh">People and AI</p>
      <details id="q-ai" name="q"><summary><h3>Do you use AI to approve claims?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>No. Meridian reads cost figures from uploaded files and purchase order details from PDFs, to save typing. A person on your claims team gives the verdict on every file and every cost line.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-self" name="q"><summary><h3>Can someone approve their own request?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>No. The person who submitted or edited a request cannot approve it, and one person takes at most one approval step per round. <a class="lk" href="/controls#c-01">See the rule <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></details>
      <details id="q-accounts" name="q"><summary><h3>Do partners and signers need accounts?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Partners use the portal for their own organization. Signatories and accounts payable work outside Meridian: they act from an emailed link or a mailbox, and need no account. <a class="lk" href="/for-partners">What partners see <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></details>
      <details id="q-support" name="q"><summary><h3>What support do we get?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Support is available to every partner and team member using Meridian, including help with access, submissions, reviews, documents and claims.</p></div></details>
    </div>
    <div class="qg" id="g-security" data-g="security"><p class="qgh">Security and data</p>
      <details id="q-staff" name="q"><summary><h3>Can Meridian staff see our data?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>No. Meridian staff set up your organization and have no access to your business records. Each customer's data is isolated from every other customer's.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-partners" name="q"><summary><h3>What can partners see?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>Only their own organization. Partners never see internal notes, internal reasons, budgets or other partners. <a class="lk" href="/controls#c-16">See the rule <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></details>
      <details id="q-files" name="q"><summary><h3>Can a file be changed after upload?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p>No. Uploaded files are fingerprinted and cannot be altered after upload. The fingerprint is kept on the record. <a class="lk" href="/audit-evidence-pack">See it on a record <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></details>
      <details id="q-cert" name="q"><summary><h3>Do you have SOC 2 or ISO 27001?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p><span class="st w">To confirm</span> This answer is being confirmed with the team. We will not claim a certification here until it is. <a class="lk" href="/trust#pending">What else is being confirmed <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></details>
    </div>
    <div class="qg" id="g-connect" data-g="connect"><p class="qgh">Connections</p>
      <details id="q-sso" name="q"><summary><h3>Do you support single sign-on?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p><span class="st">Today</span> Sign-in is by invitation, with a one-time emailed link. Access is granted per person, per Workspace, per role. Signatories act by secure link, with no account.</p><p><span class="st v">Planned</span> Sign-in through your corporate identity provider.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-crm" name="q"><summary><h3>Does it connect to our CRM, ERP or procurement system?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p><span class="st">Today</span> The CRM campaign ID and budget-tool ID are recorded on each activity, and the purchase order's number and date are read from its PDF, for the claims team to check.</p><p><span class="st v">Planned</span> Connections to your CRM, for partner and account context and campaign and pipeline data, and to your budget planning tool.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-esign" name="q"><summary><h3>Does it work with our e-signature service?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p><span class="st">Today</span> Each party signs by secure link, and the signed copy is kept on the record.</p><p><span class="st v">Planned</span> Documents routed through your own e-signature service, with signing status on the record.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-export" name="q"><summary><h3>Can we export the request list?</h3><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa"><p><span class="st">Today</span> A searchable request list, with filters by status, fiscal year and period.</p><p><span class="st v">Planned</span> Spreadsheet export of the request register.</p></div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- 3 · Close: one block of solid teal -->
<section class="close" id="walkthrough" aria-labelledby="h-close"><div class="in">
  <div class="blk pv"><h2 id="h-close">Bring the<br>hard questions.</h2><p>Invite finance, audit and security to the walkthrough. We'll answer on one of your own requests.</p><a class="btn white" href="/request-a-walkthrough">Request a walkthrough</a></div>
  <ul class="qs"><li><a href="/controls">See the controls</a></li><li><a href="/audit-evidence-pack">Open the audit evidence pack</a></li><li><a href="/how-it-works">How it works</a></li></ul>
</div></section>

</main>

<script>
  import "../scripts/questions.js";
</script>
</Base>
